messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI tools become standard in knowledge work.",
      "detail": "Productivity rises unevenly and safety debates intensify. Many jobs are redesigned rather than displaced outright."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Clean-energy investment clearly surpasses fossil fuels.",
      "detail": "Solar, wind, and storage expand as costs fall. Grid modernization and permitting become the main bottlenecks."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "EVs exceed half of new car sales globally.",
      "detail": "Urban air quality improves and oil demand growth slows. Charging access remains uneven across regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2033,
      "event": "Major climate adaptation reshapes coastal planning.",
      "detail": "Cities commit to managed retreat and protective works. Insurance and public finance adapt to escalating risks."
    },
    {
      "year": 2036,
      "event": "A new pandemic is contained relatively quickly.",
      "detail": "Surveillance and rapid vaccine platforms shorten the disruption. Global coordination improves compared with COVID-19."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "First permanently crewed lunar base operates.",
      "detail": "It supports science and resource processing. International and commercial partnerships reduce costs."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Crewed mission reaches Mars and returns.",
      "detail": "Short-stay surface ops validate in-situ resource use. Settlement remains limited by cost, radiation, and psychology."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "World population peaks near 10 billion.",
      "detail": "Aging and education-driven fertility decline slow growth. Policy shifts emphasize productivity, care, and migration."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Electricity becomes predominantly low-carbon globally.",
      "detail": "Renewables dominate with firm support from nuclear, hydro, and demand flexibility. Long-duration storage and transmission smooth variability."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "General-purpose AI copilots pervade most industries.",
      "detail": "Workflows and education adapt to human-AI teams. Safety and liability frameworks mature after early incidents."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "Carbon removal reaches gigaton scale.",
      "detail": "Nature-based and engineered methods deploy with monitoring. Removals complement, not replace, deep emissions cuts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Climate migration persists for decades.",
      "detail": "Low-lying regions lose population while inland and higher latitudes grow. New compacts manage movement and rights."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Synthetic foods supply much of global protein.",
      "detail": "Precision fermentation and cell ag reduce land use and emissions. Rural economies transition with support and new crops."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "Biodiversity stabilizes in many regions.",
      "detail": "Restoration, corridors, and invasive control show results. Extinction debt remains but trends improve."
    },
    {
      "year": 2095,
      "event": "A cyber-space crisis is de-escalated.",
      "detail": "Anti-satellite incidents and AI-accelerated cyberattacks expose vulnerabilities. Verification tools and norms avert full-scale war."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Warming stabilizes near 2–3°C.",
      "detail": "Sea levels keep rising for centuries and extremes intensify. Adaptation is mainstreamed into planning and finance."
    },
    {
      "year": 2125,
      "event": "Fusion and advanced fission add firm power.",
      "detail": "They complement renewables where geography limits options. Costs and supply chains constrain universal adoption."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Moon and Mars settlements persist semi-autonomously.",
      "detail": "They close many life-support loops yet import high-tech parts. Value lies in science, prestige, and redundancy."
    },
    {
      "year": 2180,
      "event": "Many cancers and monogenic disorders are manageable.",
      "detail": "Screening and gene editing cut mortality. Longevity improves, bounded by complex aging biology."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Cities close material loops with autonomous industry.",
      "detail": "Urban mines and circular design reduce extraction. Some critical minerals still need new sources, including space."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Large orbital habitats host tens of thousands.",
      "detail": "They serve research, industry, and tourism. Most people still live on Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Sea level stands several meters higher than 2000.",
      "detail": "Megaprojects, retreats, and floating districts are common. Historic shorelines are transformed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2350,
      "event": "Uncrewed interstellar probes return nearby data.",
      "detail": "Beamed sails and fusion-pulse concepts mature. Data arrives decades to centuries after launch."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Languages and cultures diverge markedly from today.",
      "detail": "Digital preservation keeps classics accessible. New religions and philosophies emerge."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "CO2 declines but remains above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Natural sinks and removals draw carbon down slowly. Glaciation is suppressed relative to past cycles."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "A regional asteroid impact occurs without global collapse.",
      "detail": "Surveys enable partial evacuation and mitigation. The event accelerates planetary defense investment."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Ecosystems recover under climate stabilization.",
      "detail": "Forests shift ranges and wetlands migrate inland where allowed. Conservation focuses on connectivity and refugia."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Knowledge persists through institutional redundancy.",
      "detail": "Continental and orbital archives bridge disruptions. Periodic recoveries restore lost records."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Humans adopt modest, mainstream augmentations.",
      "detail": "Enhancements are common but bounded by ethics and risk. Diversity of forms and lifestyles increases."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Some off-world polities become basically self-sufficient.",
      "detail": "They produce food, water, and habitat materials locally. Cultural divergence from Earth deepens."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "Earth is cooler than 2100 yet warmer than preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Carbon drawdown and feedbacks moderate extremes; sea level stays high. Inland megacities thrive as old coasts transform."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Long-horizon outcomes diverge across scenarios.",
      "detail": "Cumulative risks and resilience measures compete over millennia. Persistence of human or human-descended cultures seems plausible but not assured."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Humanity likely navigates a turbulent century of climate adaptation, AI integration, and demographic shifts, then gradually stabilizes with diversified energy, food, and governance systems. Off-world footholds, knowledge stewardship, and planetary defense increase resilience, while cumulative tail risks persist. By year 10000, continued human presence is plausible but not guaranteed."
}
